course: dictionary
lesson: 16088
title: Words for the same place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one country, and people in other places use a different word for the same thing. Read the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Excuse me, where is the washroom?» asks a visitor in a shop. The sentence is about a place, and the word washroom tells you where to go.
explain: The same kind of room has different names in different countries. In Canada, washroom is an everyday word. In the UK people say «toilet» or «loo», and in the US they say «bathroom» or «restroom». When you hear a word that is new to you, ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Washroom can also mean a room for washing clothes. «The laundry is in the washroom in the basement.» The clue is laundry, which means dirty clothes that need washing, so this washroom is a room for washing.
fact: Washroom is a noun. One washroom, two washrooms.
fact: «Washroom» means a room with toilets and washbasins, or a toilet or restroom.
fact: Washroom is a very common everyday word in Canada and the US.
fact: In the UK people say «toilet» or «loo», and in the US «bathroom» or «restroom».
fact: Some washrooms are rooms for washing laundry, which means dirty clothes that need cleaning. Always wash your hands with soap after using the washroom.
exercise: «May I go to the washroom, please?» What is a washroom? | A room for sleeping | *A room with toilets and washbasins | A kitchen for cooking dinner
exercise: In the UK people say «loo» for this room. What do Americans often say instead? | Garden | Playground | *Restroom
exercise: «The laundry is in the washroom in the basement.» What is the washroom used for here? | Playing games | Eating lunch | Watching television | *Washing clothes
test: Hygiene: after using the washroom, what should you do? | Eat a snack without washing | Dry your shoes | Run out and play straight away | *Wash your hands with soap
test: A child in the UK hears «Where is the washroom?» and wants the same room. Which word would she use? | Garage | Bedroom | *Toilet
exam: Which sentence is true? | Washroom means a bedroom | A washroom is a room only for animals | *A washroom can be a room with toilets and washbasins | A washroom is always a kitchen
